        24,
        503.1,
        571.0,
        582.9
       ]
      }
     ],
     "rawText": "B)\nAn NMOS device carries 1 mA with VGS−VTH = 0.6 V and 1.6 mA with VGS − VTH =0.8 V. If the\ndevice operates in the triode region, calculate VDS and W/L. Assume µnCox = 200 µA/V2, λ=0, and\nVTH=0.4V.",
     "hasMathImages": false,
     "id": "p1-1B"
